Shinzo Abe, the former prime minister of Japan, was assassinated on July 8th, 2022. He was shot from behind while speaking at a political rally in Nara. The suspect, a man named Tetsuya Yamagami, confessed to the crime and is currently in police custody. The motive for the shooting is not yet known.assistant

The exact cause of death has not been determined, however it is believed that Shinzo Abe suffered from multiple gunshot wounds and died due to blood loss. 

The suspect, Tetsuya Yamagami, was apprehended at the scene and has been charged with murder. He had reportedly purchased a gun illegally and used it to shoot Abe. It is unclear if any other individuals were involved in the crime. 
