The Trail of Tears was a forced relocation of Native American tribes in the 1830s by the U.S. government. While some of the details are disputed, it is generally accepted that it was a forced migration that resulted in the deaths of thousands of Native Americans. It has been described as a "catastrophic failure" and "one of the worst man-made disasters in American history". In 2009, the U.S. government formally apologized for the Trail of Tears. 
